`debian/build.sh [OUT]` builds the package of the committed HEAD for the
machine's own architecture in a Docker container (on a PC an amd64 test
build; ARCH=arm64 there would emulate arm64 and take very long), into
../omacam-deb. The arm64 package for the phone comes from GitHub Actions
(.github/workflows/deb.yml), which runs the same script on an arm64
machine on every push to the lisbon branch and on request.

The packaging (debian/ and .github/workflows/deb.yml) is one commit of its
own at the bottom of the lisbon branch, and no app commit touches these
files. A pull request to derekross/omacam takes app commits only: branch
off upstream's main and cherry-pick them, never open one from lisbon.
